He left us the alleys where dark sedans wait,  
The blonde who is deadly, the clock at the gate.  
He taught the raw gutter to sing like a choir,  
And wrapped the detective in classical fire.  
The writer is quiet, the glass has run dry,  
But his beautiful prose is a permanent sky.
